(Chapter 1: Process Scheduling and CPU Dispatching) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Process scheduling is the foundational activity of multiprogramming systems.) Tj
T*
(The CPU scheduler selects from processes in memory ready to execute.) Tj
T*
(In preemptive scheduling, a process can be interrupted by a timer.) Tj
T*
(Round Robin \(RR\) scheduling assigns a fixed time quantum q.) Tj
T*
(If the time quantum is too large, Round Robin degenerates into FCFS.) Tj
T*
(If the time quantum is extremely small, context switch overhead dominates.) Tj
T*
(Consequently, context switch overhead dominates overall CPU utilization.) Tj
ET
endstream
