(Chapter 2: Virtual Memory and Demand Paging) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Virtual memory is a memory management technique for storage abstraction.) Tj
T*
(Demand paging brings pages into physical memory only when referenced.) Tj
T*
(When a process accesses an invalid page, hardware triggers a page fault.) Tj
T*
(The operating system trap handler locates the missing frame on swap disk.) Tj
T*
(Effective Memory Access Time is calculated using page fault service time.) Tj
T*
(The Translation Lookaside Buffer \(TLB\) acts as a high-speed hardware cache.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
