18 TL
(Chapter 3: Page Replacement Algorithms and Thrashing) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(When memory is completely occupied, the OS executes page replacement.) Tj
T*
(The Optimal Page Replacement algorithm \(OPT\) replaces the longest unused page.) Tj
T*
(Least Recently Used \(LRU\) associates with each page the timestamp of access.) Tj
T*
(FIFO replacement suffers from Beladys Anomaly with increased page faults.) Tj
T*
(Thrashing occurs when a process spends more time paging than executing.) Tj
T*
(The Working Set Model tracks the set of actively referenced pages.) Tj
ET
endstream
